{"meta":{"templateCredsSetupCompleted":false},"name":"Compare personal grocery inflation to official CPI from receipt photos with Gemini and Telegram","nodes":[{"id":"bef8aabb-7122-5593-9a72-590089ab41f6","name":"Note: About this template","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[-620,-440],"parameters":{"color":1,"width":560,"height":1060,"content":"## Track your personal grocery inflation from receipts\n\nSend receipt photos and get **your own inflation rate**, set next to the official one for the same months. For households, budget coaches, community groups and economics teachers who suspect the official number misses what they pay.\n\n### How it works\n1. Receipts arrive from the web form or Telegram (`/sample` and `/report` also work there).\n2. Gemini reads each photo into store, date and line items.\n3. Text seen before is matched instantly. An AI agent identifies only new lines, so \"FW LG EGGS 12CT\" and \"EGGS LARGE DZ\" count as the same product.\n4. Code does the maths: price per unit, weighted by your spending (the method statistics offices use). No number comes from a model.\n5. The official index is fetched live from the US BLS (no key needed).\n6. Gemini writes an economist's note, ElevenLabs reads it aloud, and the reply goes back where the receipts came from.\n\n### Setup (about 5 minutes)\n1. Add a **Google Gemini** credential to the 2 Gemini nodes (free key at aistudio.google.com). The form needs nothing else.\n2. Optional voice: an **ElevenLabs** Header Auth credential (name `xi-api-key`) on *Speak the note*.\n3. Optional Telegram: add a @BotFather bot token to the 3 Telegram nodes, or delete them.\n4. Click **Test workflow** on the form trigger and choose *Try the sample household*.\n\nThe Data Table is created on the first run.\n\n### Customization tips\nChange the official series, currency or narrator voice in **Settings**.\n\n_Built by Alicia Graham, economist and n8n Ambassador._"},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"dd069b8e-d024-5b92-976e-67e3fea0e1b6","name":"Note: Intake","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[0,-300],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":1340,"height":760,"content":"## 1. Receipts come in\nFrom the web form or Telegram. **Gather receipts** sends photos, the sample, `/report` and anything else down the right path."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"bb689afc-6166-525d-abb5-888c2e101279","name":"Note: Reading and matching","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[1380,-300],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":1560,"height":1060,"content":"## 2. Reading and matching\nGemini reads each photo. Known receipt text matches instantly; the AI agent only names new products. Prices always come straight off the receipt."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"3f05f754-1fea-5abb-b2cc-2ec6497a5986","name":"Note: The maths","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[2980,-300],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":520,"height":760,"content":"## 3. The economist's maths\nYour inflation for your two latest months (price per unit, spending-weighted), beside the live official index."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"e0ec1b0e-883a-539c-be89-c8098951499d","name":"Note: Report","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[3540,-300],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":1740,"height":1060,"content":"## 4. The report\nGemini writes the note, ElevenLabs voices it, code builds the page or Telegram reply. Any failure falls back to plain text."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"d788bc7b-f567-50e8-b0c4-2848075f6c63","name":"Your receipts","type":"n8n-nodes-base.formTrigger","position":[60,-40],"webhookId":"e056c7a3-c8d0-5f4c-824e-b7aecccba9c2","parameters":{"options":{"buttonLabel":"Show me my inflation"},"formTitle":"Your Inflation Isn't Their Inflation","formFields":{"values":[{"fieldType":"dropdown","fieldLabel":"Where should the receipts come from?","fieldOptions":{"values":[{"option":"Try the sample household (no upload needed)"},{"option":"Use the photos I upload below"}]},"requiredField":true},{"fieldType":"file","fieldLabel":"Receipt photos","multipleFiles":true,"acceptFileTypes":".jpg, .jpeg, .png, .webp"},{"fieldLabel":"Household name","placeholder":"e.g. the-grahams (keeps your history separate)"}]},"formDescription":"Upload grocery receipt photos from at least two different months, and I'll work out how much prices went up for YOUR basket and compare it with the official number. No receipts handy? Pick the sample household."},"typeVersion":2.3},{"id":"39e66c83-b89d-507a-9cf3-ee85d34ca88d","name":"Telegram receipts","type":"n8n-nodes-base.telegramTrigger","position":[60,200],"webhookId":"90760343-9d31-54b8-8fd2-6f37d9001dae","parameters":{"updates":["message"],"additionalFields":{"download":true,"imageSize":"extraLarge"}},"typeVersion":1.2},{"id":"3a2c3abb-a4e4-5fc1-bc8d-8b5ebb878107","name":"Settings","type":"n8n-nodes-base.set","position":[300,80],"parameters":{"mode":"manual","options":{},"assignments":{"assignments":[{"id":"a3","name":"official_source","type":"string","value":"BLS"},{"id":"a4","name":"official_series_id","type":"string","value":"CUUR0000SAF11"},{"id":"a5","name":"official_label","type":"string","value":"Official US inflation: food at home"},{"id":"a6","name":"fallback_official_monthly_pct","type":"string","value":""},{"id":"a7","name":"currency_symbol","type":"string","value":"$"},{"id":"a8","name":"narrator_voice","type":"string","value":"A warm, plain-spoken economist with a light Caribbean lilt. Kind, a little funny, never preachy, zero jargon."},{"id":"a9","name":"elevenlabs_voice_id","type":"string","value":"Xb7hH8MSUJpSbSDYk0k2"},{"id":"a10","name":"elevenlabs_model","type":"string","value":"eleven_multilingual_v2"}]}},"typeVersion":3.4},{"id":"d1f3d230-3ab8-53d2-9b93-c610182f10ae","name":"Create receipt lines table","type":"n8n-nodes-base.dataTable","position":[520,80],"parameters":{"columns":{"column":[{"name":"line_id","type":"string"},{"name":"household_id","type":"string"},{"name":"receipt_id","type":"string"},{"name":"purchase_date","type":"string"},{"name":"month","type":"string"},{"name":"store","type":"string"},{"name":"raw_text","type":"string"},{"name":"item_key","type":"string"},{"name":"label","type":"string"},{"name":"category","type":"string"},{"name":"quantity","type":"number"},{"name":"line_total","type":"number"},{"name":"unit_price","type":"number"},{"name":"needs_review","type":"boolean"}]},"options":{"createIfNotExists":true},"resource":"table","operation":"create","tableName":"receipt_economist_lines"},"executeOnce":true,"typeVersion":1.1},{"id":"120991f5-0d42-5e1c-b259-82e07b85fde2","name":"Load saved lines","type":"n8n-nodes-base.dataTable","position":[740,80],"parameters":{"resource":"row","operation":"get","returnAll":true,"dataTableId":{"__rl":true,"mode":"name","value":"receipt_economist_lines"}},"executeOnce":true,"typeVersion":1.1,"alwaysOutputData":true},{"id":"86410edf-73c5-51b5-99a9-5ea19dc8c835","name":"Gather receipts","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[960,80],"parameters":{"jsCode":"// Works out who sent what, from which app, and turns it into items the rest of the workflow understands:\n//   photo   → one item per receipt image (image in binary \"data\"), read by Gemini next\n//   receipt → the sample household's receipts (already typed), straight to matching\n//   report  → no new receipts, just recalculate from what's already saved\n//   help    → nothing to read; reply with instructions\n// Every item carries the same context (channel, household, how to reply) for the nodes downstream.\nconst slug = v => String(v || '').toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').replace(/^-|-$/g, '');\nconst isImage = file => file && String(file.mimeType || '').startsWith('image/');\n\n// When should a Telegram reply be a voice note, and when is a quick text enough?\n// Telegram sends every photo of an album as its own message, so each one runs this workflow separately.\n// A voice note for each would be a lot, so album photos get a short text and /report brings the voice note.\nfunction replyStyleFor(mode, message) {\n  if (mode === 'help') return 'text';\n  if (mode === 'photos' && message.media_group_id) return 'text';\n  return 'voice';\n}\n\nlet ctx, photos = [];\n\nif ($('Telegram receipts').isExecuted) {\n  const trigger = $('Telegram receipts').first();\n  const message = trigger.json.message || {};\n  const text = String(message.text || message.caption || '').trim().toLowerCase();\n  if (isImage(trigger.binary?.data)) photos.push({ name: `telegram-${message.message_id}`, file: trigger.binary.data });\n\n  const mode = /^\\/?sample/.test(text) ? 'sample' : photos.length ? 'photos' : /^\\/?report/.test(text) ? 'report' : 'help';\n  ctx = {\n    channel: 'telegram',\n    chat_id: message.chat?.id,\n    mode,\n    reply_style: replyStyleFor(mode, message),\n    household_id: mode === 'sample' ? 'sample-household' : `telegram-${message.chat?.id}`,\n  };\n} else {\n  const answers = $('Your receipts').first().json;\n  const wantsSample = String(answers['Where should the receipts come from?'] || '').startsWith('Try');\n  for (const item of $('Your receipts').all()) {\n    for (const [key, file] of Object.entries(item.binary || {})) {\n      if (isImage(file)) photos.push({ name: file.fileName || key, file });\n    }\n  }\n  ctx = {\n    channel: 'form',\n    mode: wantsSample ? 'sample' : photos.length ? 'photos' : 'help',\n    reply_style: 'page',\n    household_id: wantsSample ? 'sample-household' : slug(answers['Household name']) || 'my-household',\n  };\n}\n\nif (ctx.mode === 'sample') {\n  return sampleHousehold().map(r => ({ json: { kind: 'receipt', ...ctx, ...r } }));\n}\nif (ctx.mode === 'photos') {\n  return photos.map((p, i) => ({ json: { kind: 'photo', ...ctx, photo_name: p.name, photo_index: i }, binary: { data: p.file } }));\n}\nreturn [{ json: { kind: ctx.mode, ...ctx } }];\n\n// Two months of invented receipts from a sample household (no real people or purchases).\n// The same products are printed differently at the two stores, on purpose.\nfunction sampleHousehold() {\n  return [\n   {\n    \"receipt_id\": \"s-0703\",\n    \"store\": \"FRESHWAY MARKET #214\",\n    \"purchase_date\": \"2026-07-03\",\n    \"lines\": [\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"FW LG EGGS 12CT\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 3.2\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"FW 2% MLK GAL\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 3.98\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"FW WHT BRD 20OZ\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 2.79\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"BANANAS LB\",\n      \"quantity\": 2.4,\n      \"line_total\": 1.49\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"MRNG BLND GRND COF 12OZ\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 8.99\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"PLANTAIN GRN EA\",\n      \"quantity\": 4,\n      \"line_total\": 3.16\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"receipt_id\": \"s-0708\",\n    \"store\": \"CORNER GROCER\",\n    \"purchase_date\": \"2026-07-08\",\n    \"lines\": [\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"BEEF GROUND 1 LB\",\n      \"quantity\": 2,\n      \"line_total\": 10.98\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"RICE LONG GRAIN 5#\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 6.49\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"CHEDDAR SHARP 8OZ\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 3.49\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"ORANGE JCE 52 OZ\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 4.29\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"DISHWASH LIQUID\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 3.29\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"receipt_id\": \"s-0714\",\n    \"store\": \"FRESHWAY MARKET #214\",\n    \"purchase_date\": \"2026-07-14\",\n    \"lines\": [\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"FW LG EGGS 12CT\",\n      \"quantity\": 2,\n      \"line_total\": 6.4\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"CHKN THGH BNLS LB\",\n      \"quantity\": 3.1,\n      \"line_total\": 9.27\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"FW 2% MLK GAL\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 3.98\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"BATH TSSU 12 DBL\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 8.99\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"BANANAS LB\",\n      \"quantity\": 2.0,\n      \"line_total\": 1.24\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"receipt_id\": \"s-0719\",\n    \"store\": \"CORNER GROCER\",\n    \"purchase_date\": \"2026-07-19\",\n    \"lines\": [\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"COFFEE GROUND MB 12Z\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 8.99\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"BREAD WHITE LOAF\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 2.79\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"PLANTAINS GREEN\",\n      \"quantity\": 6,\n      \"line_total\": 4.74\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"MILK 2PCT 1G\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 3.98\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"receipt_id\": \"s-0724\",\n    \"store\": \"FRESHWAY MARKET #214\",\n    \"purchase_date\": \"2026-07-24\",\n    \"lines\": [\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"GRND BF 80/20 1LB\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 5.49\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"FW LG EGGS 12CT\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 3.2\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"OJ NO PULP 52OZ\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 4.29\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"FW SHRP CHDR 8Z\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 3.49\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"receipt_id\": \"s-0730\",\n    \"store\": \"CORNER GROCER\",\n    \"purchase_date\": \"2026-07-30\",\n    \"lines\": [\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"CHICKEN THIGH B/L\",\n      \"quantity\": 2.6,\n      \"line_total\": 7.77\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"BANANA /LB\",\n      \"quantity\": 1.8,\n      \"line_total\": 1.12\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"RICE LONG GRAIN 5#\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 6.49\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"EGGS LARGE DZ\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 3.2\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"receipt_id\": \"s-0802\",\n    \"store\": \"CORNER GROCER\",\n    \"purchase_date\": \"2026-08-02\",\n    \"lines\": [\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"EGGS LARGE DZ\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 4.1\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"MILK 2PCT 1G\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 3.98\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"BREAD WHITE LOAF\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 2.69\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"BANANA /LB\",\n      \"quantity\": 2.2,\n      \"line_total\": 1.36\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"COFFEE GROUND MB 12Z\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 10.49\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"PLANTAINS GREEN\",\n      \"quantity\": 4,\n      \"line_total\": 3.56\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"receipt_id\": \"s-0807\",\n    \"store\": \"FRESHWAY MARKET #214\",\n    \"purchase_date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n    \"lines\": [\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"GRND BF 80/20 1LB\",\n      \"quantity\": 2,\n      \"line_total\": 11.78\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"FW SHRP CHDR 8Z\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 3.49\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"OJ NO PULP 52OZ\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 4.59\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"DISH LIQ ORIG 19OZ\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 3.29\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"LNG GRN RICE 5LB\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 6.49\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"receipt_id\": \"s-0813\",\n    \"store\": \"CORNER GROCER\",\n    \"purchase_date\": \"2026-08-13\",\n    \"lines\": [\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"EGGS LARGE DZ\",\n      \"quantity\": 2,\n      \"line_total\": 8.2\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"CHICKEN THIGH B/L\",\n      \"quantity\": 2.9,\n      \"line_total\": 8.96\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"MILK 2PCT 1G\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 3.98\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"TOILET TISSUE 12R\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 8.99\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"ITM 4471 ### ##\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 2.49\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"receipt_id\": \"s-0818\",\n    \"store\": \"FRESHWAY MARKET #214\",\n    \"purchase_date\": \"2026-08-18\",\n    \"lines\": [\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"MRNG BLND GRND COF 12OZ\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 10.49\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"FW WHT BRD 20OZ\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 2.69\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"PLANTAIN GRN EA\",\n      \"quantity\": 5,\n      \"line_total\": 4.45\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"FW 2% MLK GAL\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 3.98\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"BANANAS LB\",\n      \"quantity\": 2.1,\n      \"line_total\": 1.3\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"receipt_id\": \"s-0823\",\n    \"store\": \"CORNER GROCER\",\n    \"purchase_date\": \"2026-08-23\",\n    \"lines\": [\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"BEEF GROUND 1 LB\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 5.89\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"EGGS LARGE DZ\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 4.1\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"ORANGE JCE 52 OZ\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 4.59\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"CHEDDAR SHARP 8OZ\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 3.49\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"receipt_id\": \"s-0829\",\n    \"store\": \"FRESHWAY MARKET #214\",\n    \"purchase_date\": \"2026-08-29\",\n    \"lines\": [\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"CHKN THGH BNLS LB\",\n      \"quantity\": 2.4,\n      \"line_total\": 7.42\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"BANANAS LB\",\n      \"quantity\": 1.9,\n      \"line_total\": 1.18\n     },\n     {\n      \"raw_text\": \"FW LG EGGS 12CT\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"line_total\": 4.1\n     }\n    ]\n   }\n  ];\n}\n"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"0f0074fc-0731-588e-86f7-7ed7ba57eaab","name":"What came in?","type":"n8n-nodes-base.switch","position":[1180,80],"parameters":{"rules":{"values":[{"outputKey":"Photos to read","conditions":{"options":{"version":2,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"loose"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"30f0fc57-a331-4c88-90bc-e0b4cfb0067e","operator":{"type":"string","operation":"equals"},"leftValue":"={{ $json.kind }}","rightValue":"photo"}]},"renameOutput":true},{"outputKey":"Sample receipts","conditions":{"options":{"version":2,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"loose"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"f8768679-93db-4860-98bd-5f210f905cbe","operator":{"type":"string","operation":"equals"},"leftValue":"={{ $json.kind }}","rightValue":"receipt"}]},"renameOutput":true},{"outputKey":"Just the report","conditions":{"options":{"version":2,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"loose"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"e6da39a5-7492-4228-9fe3-91d1dab80118","operator":{"type":"string","operation":"equals"},"leftValue":"={{ $json.kind }}","rightValue":"report"}]},"renameOutput":true},{"outputKey":"Help","conditions":{"options":{"version":2,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"loose"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"67c3100a-29d9-4701-8ffb-517878ff3870","operator":{"type":"string","operation":"equals"},"leftValue":"={{ $json.kind }}","rightValue":"help"}]},"renameOutput":true}]},"options":{}},"typeVersion":3.2},{"id":"7dc14d47-09a7-51ab-84bc-6b5d63796c05","name":"Read receipt photo","type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm","onError":"continueRegularOutput","maxTries":2,"position":[1440,-60],"parameters":{"text":"Read this grocery receipt. Return the store name, the purchase date and one entry per purchased product line. Skip subtotals, tax, payment, change, loyalty savings and bag fees. If a line shows a quantity or weight (e.g. '2 @ 3.99' or '2.4 lb @ 0.62/lb'), put that in quantity and the line's amount in line_total.","messages":{"messageValues":[{"type":"HumanMessagePromptTemplate","messageType":"imageBinary","binaryImageDataKey":"data"}]},"promptType":"define","hasOutputParser":true},"retryOnFail":true,"typeVersion":1.7},{"id":"7a6ca803-b975-514f-9afd-591eca097bd6","name":"Gemini (reads & matches)","type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGoogleGemini","position":[1860,520],"parameters":{"options":{"temperature":0},"modelName":"models/gemini-3.8-flash"},"typeVersion":1.1},{"id":"02f600db-7bf0-506a-8da8-1c37ff9a3031","name":"Receipt format","type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured","position":[1600,300],"parameters":{"autoFix":true,"schemaType":"manual","inputSchema":"{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"store\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Store name as printed at the top\"\n    },\n    \"purchase_date\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"YYYY-MM-DD, or empty string if not visible\"\n    },\n    \"lines\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"raw_text\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Product text exactly as printed\"\n          },\n          \"quantity\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\",\n            \"description\": \"Units or weight bought; 1 if not shown\"\n          },\n          \"line_total\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\",\n            \"description\": \"Amount paid for this line\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"raw_text\",\n          \"quantity\",\n          \"line_total\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"store\",\n    \"purchase_date\",\n    \"lines\"\n  ]\n}"},"typeVersion":1.3},{"id":"c9c9c8cb-bbe3-57db-a3db-13d8d54b0ac3","name":"Find lines to match","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[1760,80],"parameters":{"jsCode":"// 1. Put every receipt in the same shape, whether Gemini read it from a photo or it's a typed sample receipt.\n//    A photo that can't be read doesn't stop the run; it's listed on the report instead.\n// 2. Receipt text that was identified in an earlier run is matched instantly from saved lines (no AI call).\n// 3. Only brand-new texts go to the AI agent, each unique text once, all in one batch,\n//    so it can spot that \"FW LG EGGS 12CT\" and \"EGGS LARGE DZ\" are the same product.\nconst photos = $('Gather receipts').all().filter(p => p.json.kind === 'photo');\nconst isDate = v => /^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$/.test(String(v || ''));\nconst norm = t => String(t || '').trim().toUpperCase();\n\nconst receipts = $input.all().map((item, i) => {\n  if (item.json.kind === 'receipt') return item.json; // sample household, already typed\n  const read = item.json.output || {};\n  const lines = (Array.isArray(read.lines) ? read.lines : [])\n    .filter(l => l && String(l.raw_text || '').trim() && Number(l.line_total) > 0)\n    .map(l => ({\n      raw_text: String(l.raw_text).trim(),\n      quantity: Number(l.quantity) > 0 ? Number(l.quantity) : 1,\n      line_total: Math.round(Number(l.line_total) * 100) / 100,\n    }));\n  const store = String(read.store || 'Unknown store');\n  const date = isDate(read.purchase_date) ? read.purchase_date : $now.toFormat('yyyy-MM-dd');\n  const cents = Math.round(lines.reduce((a, l) => a + l.line_total, 0) * 100);\n  return {\n    // Same store + date + total = same receipt, so sending a photo twice doesn't count it twice\n    receipt_id: `photo-${store.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-')}-${date}-${cents}`,\n    store,\n    purchase_date: date,\n    date_was_guessed: !isDate(read.purchase_date),\n    photo_name: photos[i]?.json.photo_name || `photo ${i + 1}`,\n    lines,\n  };\n});\nconst readable = receipts.filter(r => r.lines.length > 0);\n\n// What earlier runs already know: receipt text → product (only confident, reviewed-clean lines)\nconst known = {};\nfor (const row of $('Load saved lines').all().map(i => i.json)) {\n  if (row.raw_text && row.item_key && row.item_key !== 'unknown' && !(row.needs_review === true || row.needs_review === 'true')) {\n    known[norm(row.raw_text)] = { item_key: row.item_key, label: row.label, category: row.category };\n  }\n}\n\nconst unmatched = new Map();\nfor (const receipt of readable) {\n  for (const line of receipt.lines) {\n    const key = norm(line.raw_text);\n    if (!known[key] && !unmatched.has(key)) unmatched.set(key, { raw_text: line.raw_text, store: receipt.store });\n  }\n}\nconst stores = [...new Set([...unmatched.values()].map(u => u.store))];\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    receipts: readable,\n    unreadable_photos: receipts.filter(r => !r.lines.length).map(r => r.photo_name),\n    readable_count: readable.length,\n    known: Object.fromEntries(readable.flatMap(r => r.lines).map(l => [norm(l.raw_text), known[norm(l.raw_text)]]).filter(([, v]) => v)),\n    unmatched_count: unmatched.size,\n    // Grouped under store headings so store names don't leak into the text the model copies back\n    unmatched_list: stores.map(store => `${store}:\\n` + [...unmatched.values()].filter(u => u.store === store).map(u => `- ${u.raw_text}`).join('\\n')).join('\\n\\n'),\n  },\n}];\n"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"9f11bf53-78c7-5959-bb65-08999f83cbe1","name":"Anything new to match?","type":"n8n-nodes-base.switch","position":[1980,80],"parameters":{"rules":{"values":[{"outputKey":"New to me","conditions":{"options":{"version":2,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"loose"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"b4b01834-effd-42b5-82be-9ee5f86b89a0","operator":{"type":"number","operation":"gt"},"leftValue":"={{ $json.unmatched_count }}","rightValue":0}]},"renameOutput":true},{"outputKey":"All remembered","conditions":{"options":{"version":2,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"loose"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"02182810-495a-4432-8d58-5bedde6434a7","operator":{"type":"number","operation":"equals"},"leftValue":"={{ $json.unmatched_count }}","rightValue":0},{"id":"cd33ab34-444d-4374-b879-e4a8fded357d","operator":{"type":"number","operation":"gt"},"leftValue":"={{ $json.readable_count }}","rightValue":0}]},"renameOutput":true},{"outputKey":"Couldn't read","conditions":{"options":{"version":2,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"loose"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"e6f99f57-1aeb-4a82-9ce6-dbea4e010d1f","operator":{"type":"number","operation":"equals"},"leftValue":"={{ $json.readable_count }}","rightValue":0}]},"renameOutput":true}]},"options":{}},"typeVersion":3.2},{"id":"dbdbe197-4e0b-5329-a5d1-fca135dbcbb8","name":"Match new lines to products","type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent","onError":"continueRegularOutput","maxTries":2,"position":[2240,-80],"parameters":{"text":"=These receipt lines are new to me. Identify the product for each one:\n{{ $json.unmatched_list }}","options":{"maxIterations":30,"systemMessage":"=You identify products on grocery receipts so one household's prices can be compared over time. Different stores print the same product differently (\"FW LG EGGS 12CT\" and \"EGGS LARGE DZ\" are both a dozen large eggs). The same product must ALWAYS get the same item_key.\n\nHow to work:\n1. For each product type in the list, call \"Search saved products\" with a short keyword (e.g. egg, milk, coffee). If a saved product is the same thing in the same size, reuse its item_key exactly.\n2. Otherwise create a new snake_case item_key that includes the size or unit, e.g. eggs_large_dozen, coffee_ground_12oz, bananas_per_lb. When two lines in THIS list are the same product, give them the same new item_key.\n3. Unreadable text, coupons, deposits, tax, fees or anything that isn't a product: item_key \"unknown\", needs_review true. Never guess.\n4. You only identify products. Never mention or change prices.\n\nCategories: eggs, dairy, meat_poultry_fish, fruits_vegetables, cereals_bakery, beverages, other_food, household_supplies, personal_care, other.\nReturn exactly one match per line, copying raw_text exactly as given."},"promptType":"define","hasOutputParser":true},"retryOnFail":true,"typeVersion":3.1},{"id":"eb3d2c96-12ae-5460-b12b-586e2b959ce7","name":"Search saved products","type":"n8n-nodes-base.dataTableTool","position":[2260,300],"parameters":{"limit":25,"filters":{"conditions":[{"keyName":"label","keyValue":"={{ '%' + $fromAI('keyword', 'One short product keyword, e.g. egg', 'string') + '%' }}","condition":"ilike"},{"keyName":"item_key","keyValue":"={{ '%' + $fromAI('keyword', 'One short product keyword, e.g. egg', 'string') + '%' }}","condition":"ilike"}]},"resource":"row","matchType":"anyCondition","operation":"get","dataTableId":{"__rl":true,"mode":"name","value":"receipt_economist_lines"},"descriptionType":"manual","toolDescription":"Searches products already identified on earlier receipts. Give it ONE short keyword (e.g. 'egg', 'coffee', 'plantain'). It returns saved receipt lines whose product name or key contains the keyword, with the item_key, label and category they were given. Empty result = nothing similar saved yet."},"typeVersion":1.1},{"id":"41f18e45-f704-5db9-8fcf-c246d5e0295a","name":"Matches format","type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured","position":[2420,300],"parameters":{"autoFix":true,"schemaType":"manual","inputSchema":"{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"matches\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"raw_text\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"The receipt text, copied exactly\"\n          },\n          \"item_key\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Existing or new snake_case product key with size, or 'unknown'\"\n          },\n          \"label\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Friendly product name, e.g. 'Large eggs (dozen)'\"\n          },\n          \"category\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"eggs\",\n              \"dairy\",\n              \"meat_poultry_fish\",\n              \"fruits_vegetables\",\n              \"cereals_bakery\",\n              \"beverages\",\n              \"other_food\",\n              \"household_supplies\",\n              \"personal_care\",\n              \"other\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"needs_review\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"raw_text\",\n          \"item_key\",\n          \"label\",\n          \"category\",\n          \"needs_review\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"matches\"\n  ]\n}"},"typeVersion":1.3},{"id":"eb18163b-b268-5d08-b101-d370f61931b8","name":"Price matched lines","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[2560,80],"parameters":{"jsCode":"// Put every receipt line together with its product. What earlier runs learned wins, then the AI's answer.\n// Prices, quantities and totals come straight from the receipt, so no number in the\n// report is invented by a model. Lines nobody could identify are flagged for review.\nconst found = $('Find lines to match').first().json;\nconst household = $('Gather receipts').first().json.household_id;\n// Compare texts case-insensitively, ignoring a leading \"- \" or a trailing \"(store)\" the model might echo\nconst norm = t => String(t || '').trim().replace(/^-\\s*/, '').replace(/\\s+\\([^)]*\\)$/, '').trim().toUpperCase();\n\nlet aiAnswers = [];\ntry {\n  const out = $('Match new lines to products').first().json.output;\n  aiAnswers = Array.isArray(out?.matches) ? out.matches : [];\n} catch (e) {\n  // Every line was already known, so the AI step didn't run\n}\nconst fromAi = new Map(aiAnswers.map(m => [norm(m.raw_text), m]));\n\nconst rows = [];\nfor (const receipt of found.receipts) {\n  receipt.lines.forEach((line, idx) => {\n    const hit = found.known[norm(line.raw_text)] || fromAi.get(norm(line.raw_text)) || {};\n    const key = String(hit.item_key || 'unknown').toLowerCase().trim().replace(/[^a-z0-9_]+/g, '_') || 'unknown';\n    const qty = Number(line.quantity) > 0 ? Number(line.quantity) : 1;\n    const total = Number(line.line_total) || 0;\n    rows.push({\n      json: {\n        line_id: `${household}|${receipt.receipt_id}|${idx}`,\n        household_id: household,\n        receipt_id: receipt.receipt_id,\n        purchase_date: receipt.purchase_date,\n        month: String(receipt.purchase_date).slice(0, 7),\n        store: receipt.store,\n        raw_text: line.raw_text,\n        item_key: key,\n        label: hit.label || line.raw_text,\n        category: hit.category || 'other',\n        quantity: qty,\n        line_total: Math.round(total * 100) / 100,\n        unit_price: Math.round((total / qty) * 10000) / 10000,\n        needs_review: key === 'unknown' || hit.needs_review === true,\n      },\n    });\n  });\n}\nreturn rows;\n"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"f70665c3-6125-50e2-897e-01f09d6e876a","name":"Save receipt lines","type":"n8n-nodes-base.dataTable","position":[2780,80],"parameters":{"columns":{"value":{"label":"={{ $json.label }}","month":"={{ $json.month }}","store":"={{ $json.store }}","line_id":"={{ $json.line_id }}","category":"={{ $json.category }}","item_key":"={{ $json.item_key }}","quantity":"={{ $json.quantity }}","raw_text":"={{ $json.raw_text }}","line_total":"={{ $json.line_total }}","receipt_id":"={{ $json.receipt_id }}","unit_price":"={{ $json.unit_price }}","household_id":"={{ $json.household_id }}","needs_review":"={{ $json.needs_review }}","purchase_date":"={{ $json.purchase_date }}"},"schema":[{"id":"line_id","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"line_id","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"household_id","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"household_id","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"receipt_id","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"receipt_id","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"purchase_date","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"purchase_date","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"month","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"month","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"store","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"store","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"raw_text","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"raw_text","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"item_key","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"item_key","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"label","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"label","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"category","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"category","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"quantity","type":"number","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"quantity","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"line_total","type":"number","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"line_total","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"unit_price","type":"number","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"unit_price","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"needs_review","type":"boolean","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"needs_review","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true}],"mappingMode":"defineBelow","matchingColumns":[],"attemptToConvertTypes":false,"convertFieldsToString":false},"filters":{"conditions":[{"keyName":"line_id","keyValue":"={{ $json.line_id }}","condition":"eq"}]},"options":{},"resource":"row","matchType":"allConditions","operation":"upsert","dataTableId":{"__rl":true,"mode":"name","value":"receipt_economist_lines"}},"typeVersion":1.1},{"id":"7e82c0ea-a592-5ff8-9603-3e7a0b91f796","name":"Fetch official index","type":"n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest","onError":"continueRegularOutput","maxTries":3,"position":[3040,80],"parameters":{"url":"https://api.bls.gov/publicAPI/v1/timeseries/data/","method":"POST","options":{"timeout":15000},"jsonBody":"={{ JSON.stringify({ seriesid: [$('Settings').first().json.official_series_id], startyear: String($now.year - 4), endyear: String($now.year) }) }}","sendBody":true,"specifyBody":"json"},"executeOnce":true,"retryOnFail":true,"typeVersion":4.2,"waitBetweenTries":2000},{"id":"6c729916-8ed3-53d1-bbec-6ea0b893db08","name":"Calculate personal inflation","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[3260,80],"parameters":{"jsCode":"// Personal inflation, the way a statistics office would do it (a Laspeyres-style index):\n// 1. Compare the two most recent months that have receipts.\n// 2. For every product bought in BOTH months, compare the average price per unit.\n// 3. Weight each product by what you spent on it in the earlier month.\n// Products seen in only one month can't be compared, so they're left out (the report shows coverage).\n// Then line the result up against the official index for the SAME two months.\nconst s = $('Settings').first().json;\nconst ctx = $('Gather receipts').first().json;\nconst round = (x, d = 2) => Math.round(x * 10 ** d) / 10 ** d;\nconst isTrue = v => v === true || v === 'true';\n\n// This household's history = everything saved before this run + the lines from this run\nconst byLineId = new Map();\nfor (const r of $('Load saved lines').all().map(i => i.json)) {\n  if (r.household_id === ctx.household_id) byLineId.set(r.line_id, r);\n}\ntry {\n  for (const r of $('Price matched lines').all().map(i => i.json)) byLineId.set(r.line_id, r);\n} catch (e) {\n  // A /report request: no new receipts this time, so there are no new lines\n}\nconst rows = [...byLineId.values()].filter(r => r && r.item_key && r.month);\nconst reviewRows = rows.filter(r => isTrue(r.needs_review) || r.item_key === 'unknown');\nconst priced = rows.filter(r => !reviewRows.includes(r) && Number(r.unit_price) > 0);\nconst months = [...new Set(rows.map(r => r.month))].sort();\n\nconst summary = {\n  household_id: ctx.household_id,\n  months,\n  receipts: new Set(rows.map(r => r.receipt_id)).size,\n  lines: rows.length,\n  needs_review: reviewRows.map(r => ({ raw_text: r.raw_text, store: r.store, date: r.purchase_date, amount: Number(r.line_total) })),\n  official: { label: s.official_label, change_pct: null, method: 'unavailable' },\n  gap_pts: null,\n};\n\nif (months.length < 2) {\n  return [{ json: { ...summary, status: 'needs_more_months' } }];\n}\n\nconst baseMonth = months[months.length - 2];\nconst currentMonth = months[months.length - 1];\n\n// Average price per unit = total spent / total quantity (so 2 dozen eggs count twice)\nconst avgUnitPrice = list => {\n  const qty = list.reduce((a, r) => a + Number(r.quantity || 1), 0);\n  const spent = list.reduce((a, r) => a + Number(r.line_total || 0), 0);\n  return qty > 0 ? spent / qty : 0;\n};\n\nconst byItem = {};\nfor (const r of priced) {\n  const it = (byItem[r.item_key] ||= { item_key: r.item_key, label: r.label, category: r.category, base: [], current: [] });\n  if (r.month === baseMonth) it.base.push(r);\n  if (r.month === currentMonth) it.current.push(r);\n}\n\nconst compared = Object.values(byItem)\n  .filter(i => i.base.length && i.current.length)\n  .map(i => {\n    const p0 = avgUnitPrice(i.base);\n    const p1 = avgUnitPrice(i.current);\n    return {\n      item_key: i.item_key,\n      label: i.label,\n      category: i.category,\n      price_before: round(p0),\n      price_now: round(p1),\n      change_pct: round((p1 / p0 - 1) * 100, 1),\n      weight: i.base.reduce((a, r) => a + Number(r.line_total || 0), 0),\n    };\n  });\n\nconst totalWeight = compared.reduce((a, c) => a + c.weight, 0);\nconst baseSpend = priced.filter(r => r.month === baseMonth).reduce((a, r) => a + Number(r.line_total || 0), 0);\n\nif (!compared.length || totalWeight <= 0) {\n  return [{ json: { ...summary, status: 'no_overlap', base_month: baseMonth, current_month: currentMonth } }];\n}\n\nconst personalChange = round((compared.reduce((a, c) => a + (c.weight / totalWeight) * (c.change_pct / 100), 0)) * 100, 2);\n\nfor (const c of compared) {\n  c.weight_share_pct = round((c.weight / totalWeight) * 100, 1);\n  c.contribution_pts = round((c.weight / totalWeight) * c.change_pct, 2); // share of the headline number\n}\n\nconst categories = {};\nfor (const c of compared) {\n  const cat = (categories[c.category] ||= { category: c.category, weight: 0, weighted: 0 });\n  cat.weight += c.weight;\n  cat.weighted += c.weight * c.change_pct;\n}\nconst categoryChanges = Object.values(categories)\n  .map(c => ({ category: c.category, change_pct: round(c.weighted / c.weight, 1), weight_share_pct: round((c.weight / totalWeight) * 100, 1) }))\n  .sort((a, b) => b.weight_share_pct - a.weight_share_pct);\n\ncompared.forEach(c => delete c.weight);\nconst ranked = [...compared].sort((a, b) => b.contribution_pts - a.contribution_pts);\n\n// The official number for the same two months. If the live lookup failed (offline, rate limit,\n// a country BLS doesn't cover), use the rate typed into Settings, and say so on the report.\nlet official = summary.official;\nif (s.official_source === 'BLS') {\n  const points = $input.first().json?.Results?.series?.[0]?.data || [];\n  const find = ym => points.find(p => p.year === ym.slice(0, 4) && p.period === `M${ym.slice(5, 7)}`);\n  const before = find(baseMonth);\n  const now = find(currentMonth);\n  if (before && now) {\n    official = {\n      label: s.official_label,\n      change_pct: round((Number(now.value) / Number(before.value) - 1) * 100, 2),\n      method: 'live',\n      index_before: Number(before.value),\n      index_now: Number(now.value),\n    };\n  }\n}\nconst fallback = String(s.fallback_official_monthly_pct ?? '').trim();\nif (official.change_pct === null && fallback !== '' && !isNaN(Number(fallback))) {\n  official = { label: s.official_label, change_pct: Number(fallback), method: 'fallback' };\n}\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    ...summary,\n    status: 'ok',\n    base_month: baseMonth,\n    current_month: currentMonth,\n    personal_change_pct: personalChange,\n    coverage_pct: round((totalWeight / baseSpend) * 100, 0),\n    items_compared: compared.length,\n    top_drivers: ranked.filter(c => c.contribution_pts > 0).slice(0, 3),\n    top_relief: ranked.filter(c => c.contribution_pts < 0).reverse().slice(0, 2),\n    category_changes: categoryChanges,\n    item_changes: ranked,\n    official,\n    gap_pts: official.change_pct === null ? null : round(personalChange - official.change_pct, 2),\n  },\n}];\n"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"68c4e037-82fe-5cd7-b47f-9834bb5ee312","name":"Write the economist's note","type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm","onError":"continueRegularOutput","maxTries":2,"position":[3600,80],"parameters":{"text":"=Here are the computed results for one household. Every number is already calculated. Use them exactly as given and do NOT calculate or invent any new numbers.\n\n{{ JSON.stringify({ status: $json.status, base_month: $json.base_month, current_month: $json.current_month, personal_change_pct: $json.personal_change_pct, official: $json.official, gap_pts: $json.gap_pts, top_drivers: $json.top_drivers, top_relief: $json.top_relief, category_changes: $json.category_changes, coverage_pct: $json.coverage_pct, receipts: $json.receipts, months: $json.months }, null, 1) }}\n\nIf status is 'ok': explain why their personal inflation differs from the official figure. Official figures average millions of households, and this household's basket leans on the products in top_drivers. Name the drivers with their % change. Mention relief items if any.\nIf status is 'needs_more_months' or 'no_overlap': warmly explain they need receipts from two different months with some of the same products, and what to do next.\nThe voice_note is the same story told out loud to a friend: start with their number next to the official one, then the biggest driver, then the tip. If a number rounds to zero, say it barely moved instead of reading out zero point zero.\nVoice: {{ $('Settings').first().json.narrator_voice }}","promptType":"define","hasOutputParser":true},"retryOnFail":true,"typeVersion":1.7},{"id":"a0df2e95-45a3-5fa9-9861-6c17d7712b3a","name":"Gemini (writes)","type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGoogleGemini","position":[3560,320],"parameters":{"options":{"temperature":0.7},"modelName":"models/gemini-3.8-flash"},"typeVersion":1.1},{"id":"ed4a44f8-ea5b-5e96-89db-9096f24808b2","name":"Note format","type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured","position":[3740,320],"parameters":{"autoFix":true,"schemaType":"manual","inputSchema":"{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"headline\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Max 80 characters, punchy, uses the real numbers\"\n    },\n    \"verdict\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"2-3 sentences comparing their number with the official one\"\n    },\n    \"drivers\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"maxItems\": 3,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"label\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"explanation\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"One sentence, uses the given % change\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"label\",\n          \"explanation\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"tip\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"One practical, non-preachy suggestion\"\n    },\n    \"method_note\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"One sentence on method and limits, in plain words\"\n    },\n    \"voice_note\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"What you'd say in a 30-45 second voice note, 70-110 words. Spoken style: no % or $ signs (say 'percent', 'dollars'), numbers rounded to one decimal.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"headline\",\n    \"verdict\",\n    \"drivers\",\n    \"tip\",\n    \"method_note\",\n    \"voice_note\"\n  ]\n}"},"typeVersion":1.3},{"id":"460e3d16-c275-581c-82e7-173aefa58804","name":"Voice note wanted?","type":"n8n-nodes-base.if","position":[3960,80],"parameters":{"options":{},"conditions":{"options":{"version":2,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"loose"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"50ef7ff4-7659-4cbf-9683-23f9f1ff30da","operator":{"type":"string","operation":"notEquals"},"leftValue":"={{ $('Gather receipts').first().json.reply_style }}","rightValue":"text"},{"id":"7800f0c5-3bac-41d2-889e-191a9568f383","operator":{"type":"string","operation":"notEmpty","singleValue":true},"leftValue":"={{ $('Settings').first().json.elevenlabs_voice_id }}","rightValue":""}]}},"typeVersion":2.2},{"id":"3806b85b-7fa1-5263-9a70-ee414dc40546","name":"Speak the note","type":"n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest","onError":"continueRegularOutput","maxTries":2,"position":[4180,-40],"parameters":{"url":"={{ 'https://api.elevenlabs.io/v1/text-to-speech/' + $('Settings').first().json.elevenlabs_voice_id + '?output_format=mp3_44100_64' }}","method":"POST","options":{"timeout":60000,"response":{"response":{"responseFormat":"file","outputPropertyName":"data"}}},"jsonBody":"={{ JSON.stringify({ text: $json.output?.voice_note || \"Your report is ready. The numbers are in the message.\", model_id: $('Settings').first().json.elevenlabs_model }) }}","sendBody":true,"specifyBody":"json","authentication":"genericCredentialType","genericAuthType":"httpHeaderAuth"},"retryOnFail":true,"typeVersion":4.2},{"id":"da86a40a-fe6d-5aae-96da-1af6baa733a2","name":"Build report","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[4400,80],"parameters":{"jsCode":"// Build every reply from the same numbers: a web page for the form, a message (and voice note) for Telegram.\n// Numbers come from \"Calculate personal inflation\"; the words come from the economist's note.\n// If the note step failed, a plain-English fallback is used so a reply always goes out.\nconst ctx = $('Gather receipts').first().json;\nconst input = $input.first();\nconst esc = v => String(v ?? '').replace(/[&<>\"']/g, c => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '\"': '&quot;', \"'\": '&#39;' }[c]));\nconst tryNode = (name, fallback) => { try { return $(name).first().json; } catch (e) { return fallback; } };\n\nconst HELP = [\n  \"Hi! I'm your Receipt Economist 🧾\",\n  '',\n  '• Send me a photo of a grocery receipt (one per message works best)',\n  '• /sample: try me with a sample household',\n  '• /report: hear your personal inflation next to the official number',\n  '',\n  'I need receipts from two different months to measure how prices moved.',\n].join('\\n');\n\nconst reply = text => [{ json: { ...ctx, html: `<div style=\"font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;text-align:left;white-space:pre-line\">${esc(text)}</div>`, tg_text: esc(text), has_audio: false } }];\n\nif (input.json.kind === 'help') {\n  return reply(ctx.channel === 'form'\n    ? 'No photos arrived. Attach at least one receipt photo, or pick the sample household.'\n    : HELP);\n}\nif (input.json.readable_count === 0) {\n  return reply(`I couldn't read ${input.json.unreadable_photos.length > 1 ? 'those photos' : 'that photo'}. Try a flatter, well-lit shot with the whole receipt in frame.`);\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the full report\nconst d = $('Calculate personal inflation').first().json;\nconst s = $('Settings').first().json;\nconst note = tryNode(\"Write the economist's note\", {}).output || null;\nconst found = tryNode('Find lines to match', { receipts: [], unreadable_photos: [] });\n\nconst pct = (v, digits = 1) => (v === null || v === undefined ? 'n/a' : `${v > 0 ? '+' : ''}${Number(v).toFixed(digits)}%`);\nconst money = v => `${s.currency_symbol}${Number(v).toFixed(2)}`;\nconst monthName = ym => (ym ? DateTime.fromFormat(ym, 'yyyy-MM').toFormat('LLLL yyyy') : '');\nconst CATEGORY_NAMES = {\n  eggs: 'Eggs', dairy: 'Dairy', meat_poultry_fish: 'Meat, poultry & fish', fruits_vegetables: 'Fruits & vegetables',\n  cereals_bakery: 'Cereals & bakery', beverages: 'Coffee, juice & drinks', other_food: 'Other food',\n  household_supplies: 'Household supplies', personal_care: 'Personal care', other: 'Other',\n};\n\nconst n = note || {\n  headline: d.status === 'ok' ? `Your groceries moved ${pct(d.personal_change_pct)} this month` : 'Keep those receipts coming',\n  verdict: d.status === 'ok'\n    ? `Between ${monthName(d.base_month)} and ${monthName(d.current_month)}, the things you actually buy changed price by ${pct(d.personal_change_pct, 2)}.`\n    : 'You need receipts from at least two different months before I can measure your inflation.',\n  drivers: (d.top_drivers || []).map(t => ({ label: t.label, explanation: `${pct(t.change_pct)} per unit` })),\n  tip: '',\n  method_note: '',\n};\nconst gapLine = d.gap_pts !== null && d.gap_pts !== undefined\n  ? `That's ${Math.abs(d.gap_pts).toFixed(2)} points ${d.gap_pts >= 0 ? 'above' : 'below'} the official number for the same two months.` : '';\nconst officialNote = d.official.method === 'live' ? 'same months, official index' : d.official.method === 'fallback' ? 'rate from your Settings' : 'official figure unavailable';\nconst review = [\n  ...(d.needs_review || []).map(r => `\"${r.raw_text}\" at ${r.store} (${r.date}), ${money(r.amount)}`),\n  ...(found.unreadable_photos || []).map(p => `Photo \"${p}\" couldn't be read. Try a flatter, well-lit shot.`),\n];\n\n// The voice note, if one was recorded (ElevenLabs step), travels on as binary \"data\"\nconst hasAudio = String(input.binary?.data?.mimeType || '').startsWith('audio/');\nlet audioTag = '';\nif (hasAudio && ctx.channel === 'form') {\n  const buffer = await this.helpers.getBinaryDataBuffer(0, 'data');\n  audioTag = `<p class=\"voice\">🎙️ Hear the economist's note<br><audio controls src=\"data:${input.binary.data.mimeType};base64,${buffer.toString('base64')}\"></audio></p>`;\n}\n\n// ---- Telegram: a short \"got it\" for album photos, the full story otherwise\nconst thisRun = found.receipts || [];\nlet tg;\nif (ctx.channel === 'telegram' && ctx.reply_style === 'text' && thisRun.length) {\n  const r = thisRun[0];\n  const total = r.lines.reduce((a, l) => a + l.line_total, 0);\n  tg = [\n    `✅ Got it: <b>${esc(r.store)}</b> (${esc(r.purchase_date)}), ${r.lines.length} lines, ${money(total)}.`,\n    d.status === 'ok'\n      ? `So far your inflation is <b>${pct(d.personal_change_pct, 2)}</b> vs official ${pct(d.official.change_pct, 2)} (${monthName(d.base_month)} → ${monthName(d.current_month)}).`\n      : 'I need receipts from a second month before I can measure prices.',\n    'Send more, or /report for the full voice note.',\n  ].join('\\n');\n} else {\n  tg = [\n    `<b>${esc(n.headline)}</b>`,\n    '',\n    esc(n.verdict),\n    ...(d.status === 'ok' ? [\n      '',\n      `Your inflation: <b>${pct(d.personal_change_pct, 2)}</b> (${monthName(d.base_month)} → ${monthName(d.current_month)})`,\n      `${esc(d.official.label)}: <b>${pct(d.official.change_pct, 2)}</b> (${officialNote})`,\n      esc(gapLine),\n    ] : []),\n    ...((n.drivers || []).length ? ['', \"<b>What's pushing your number</b>\", ...n.drivers.slice(0, 3).map(x => `• <b>${esc(x.label)}:</b> ${esc(x.explanation)}`)] : []),\n    ...(n.tip ? ['', '<b>One thing to try</b>', esc(n.tip)] : []),\n    ...(review.length ? ['', '<b>Please double-check these</b> (left out of the maths)', ...review.map(x => `• ${esc(x)}`)] : []),\n    ...(d.status === 'ok' ? ['', `<i>${d.items_compared} products compared, ${d.coverage_pct}% of your ${monthName(d.base_month)} spending · ${d.receipts} receipts</i>`] : []),\n  ].join('\\n').slice(0, 4000);\n}\n\n// ---- Web page for the form\nconst itemRows = (d.item_changes || []).map(i => `\n  <tr><td>${esc(i.label)}</td><td>${esc(CATEGORY_NAMES[i.category] || i.category)}</td>\n  <td class=\"r\">${money(i.price_before)}</td><td class=\"r\">${money(i.price_now)}</td>\n  <td class=\"r ${i.change_pct > 0 ? 'up' : i.change_pct < 0 ? 'down' : ''}\">${pct(i.change_pct)}</td>\n  <td class=\"r\">${i.weight_share_pct}%</td></tr>`).join('');\nconst drivers = (n.drivers || []).slice(0, 3).map(x => `<li><b>${esc(x.label)}:</b> ${esc(x.explanation)}</li>`).join('');\n\nconst html = `\n<style>\n  .re{font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto;text-align:left;line-height:1.5}\n  .re h1{font-size:1.6rem;margin:.2em 0}.re .lede{font-size:1.05rem;color:#444}\n  .re .nums{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:18px 0}\n  .re .num{flex:1 1 220px;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;background:#f4f4f7}\n  .re .num.you{background:#fff1e6;border:2px solid #ff6d2d}\n  .re .num span{display:block;font-size:.85rem;color:#555}.re .num b{display:block;font-size:2.1rem}.re .num small{color:#666}\n  .re .gap,.re .voice{background:#f4f4f7;border-radius:10px;padding:10px 14px}.re audio{width:100%;margin-top:6px}\n  .re table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.9rem;margin-top:8px}\n  .re td,.re th{border-bottom:1px solid #e5e5ea;padding:6px 4px;text-align:left}.re .r{text-align:right}\n  .re .up{color:#c2410c;font-weight:600}.re .down{color:#15803d;font-weight:600}\n  .re .muted{color:#666;font-size:.85rem}.re h2{font-size:1.1rem;margin-top:22px}\n</style>\n<div class=\"re\">\n  <h1>${esc(n.headline)}</h1>\n  <p class=\"lede\">${esc(n.verdict)}</p>\n  ${audioTag}\n  ${d.status === 'ok' ? `\n  <div class=\"nums\">\n    <div class=\"num you\"><span>Your inflation</span><b>${pct(d.personal_change_pct, 2)}</b><small>${monthName(d.base_month)} → ${monthName(d.current_month)}</small></div>\n    <div class=\"num them\"><span>${esc(d.official.label)}</span><b>${pct(d.official.change_pct, 2)}</b><small>${officialNote}</small></div>\n  </div>\n  ${gapLine ? `<p class=\"gap\">${gapLine.replace(/(\\d+\\.\\d+ points (above|below))/, '<b>$1</b>')}</p>` : ''}` : ''}\n  ${drivers ? `<h2>What's pushing your number</h2><ul>${drivers}</ul>` : ''}\n  ${n.tip ? `<h2>One thing to try</h2><p>${esc(n.tip)}</p>` : ''}\n  ${itemRows ? `<h2>Every product I could compare</h2>\n  <table><tr><th>Product</th><th>Category</th><th class=\"r\">Before</th><th class=\"r\">Now</th><th class=\"r\">Change</th><th class=\"r\">Weight</th></tr>${itemRows}</table>\n  <p class=\"muted\">${d.items_compared} products bought in both months, covering ${d.coverage_pct}% of your ${monthName(d.base_month)} spending. Weight = share of that spending.</p>` : ''}\n  ${review.length ? `<h2>Please double-check these</h2><ul>${review.map(x => `<li>${esc(x)}</li>`).join('')}</ul><p class=\"muted\">They were left out of the calculation.</p>` : ''}\n  <p class=\"muted\">${esc(n.method_note || 'Method: average price per unit for each product in both months, weighted by what you spent on it in the earlier month (a Laspeyres-style index, like the one statistics offices use). A personal index from a few receipts is noisy. Treat it as a conversation starter, not an official statistic.')}</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\">${d.receipts} receipts · ${d.lines} lines · household \"${esc(d.household_id)}\"</p>\n</div>`;\n\nreturn [{\n  json: { ...ctx, status: d.status, html, tg_text: tg, tg_caption: `🎙️ ${esc(n.headline)}`.slice(0, 1000), has_audio: hasAudio },\n  ...(hasAudio ? { binary: { data: { ...input.binary.data, fileName: 'economist-note.mp3', fileExtension: 'mp3' } } } : {}),\n}];\n"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"e320f389-c85b-546a-be73-4dc84b19cd64","name":"Reply where they asked","type":"n8n-nodes-base.switch","position":[4620,80],"parameters":{"rules":{"values":[{"outputKey":"Web form","conditions":{"options":{"version":2,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"loose"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"744456be-9496-46b0-8d09-ff49cb108d32","operator":{"type":"string","operation":"equals"},"leftValue":"={{ $json.channel }}","rightValue":"form"}]},"renameOutput":true},{"outputKey":"Telegram with voice","conditions":{"options":{"version":2,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"loose"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"66f170d5-8812-4158-890a-dda9077de8d2","operator":{"type":"string","operation":"equals"},"leftValue":"={{ $json.channel }}","rightValue":"telegram"},{"id":"e7b2ee2c-7ff4-4988-8e87-faa4d5f4664e","operator":{"type":"boolean","operation":"true","singleValue":true},"leftValue":"={{ $json.has_audio }}","rightValue":""}]},"renameOutput":true},{"outputKey":"Telegram text","conditions":{"options":{"version":2,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"loose"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"d3637fa0-5ff3-48a4-8de0-5dedda4d8003","operator":{"type":"string","operation":"equals"},"leftValue":"={{ $json.channel }}","rightValue":"telegram"},{"id":"c60ea0a8-73b1-450d-a829-cb4e093c8be0","operator":{"type":"boolean","operation":"false","singleValue":true},"leftValue":"={{ $json.has_audio }}","rightValue":""}]},"renameOutput":true}]},"options":{}},"typeVersion":3.2},{"id":"4182c93f-a4aa-582c-9f14-54a93100f32a","name":"Show the report","type":"n8n-nodes-base.form","position":[4880,-80],"webhookId":"5aa92d0e-9c17-57d2-b38a-e4e8d37aee44","parameters":{"operation":"completion","respondWith":"showText","responseText":"={{ $json.html }}"},"typeVersion":2.3},{"id":"f7d1adb5-4948-525f-8ca2-282caa2439c8","name":"Telegram: send voice note","type":"n8n-nodes-base.telegram","onError":"continueRegularOutput","position":[4880,100],"webhookId":"fdb71fca-4753-542f-a143-95a72658b32e","parameters":{"chatId":"={{ $json.chat_id }}","resource":"message","operation":"sendAudio","binaryData":true,"additionalFields":{"title":"Your economist's note","caption":"={{ $json.tg_caption }}","performer":"Receipt Economist","parse_mode":"HTML"},"binaryPropertyName":"data"},"typeVersion":1.2},{"id":"8890ec9f-4639-5a94-ab8e-93b6bb85e50e","name":"Telegram: send report","type":"n8n-nodes-base.telegram","onError":"continueRegularOutput","position":[5100,260],"webhookId":"725d741a-8c65-5fc3-9e7d-435f6d75c97c","parameters":{"text":"={{ $('Build report').first().json.tg_text }}","chatId":"={{ $('Build report').first().json.chat_id }}","resource":"message","operation":"sendMessage","additionalFields":{"parse_mode":"HTML","appendAttribution":false,"disable_web_page_preview":true}},"typeVersion":1.2}],"settings":{"executionOrder":"v1"},"connections":{"Settings":{"main":[[{"node":"Create receipt lines table","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Note format":{"ai_outputParser":[[{"node":"Write the economist's note","type":"ai_outputParser","index":0}]]},"Build report":{"main":[[{"node":"Reply where they asked","type":"main","index":0}]]},"What came in?":{"main":[[{"node":"Read receipt photo","type":"main","index":0}],[{"node":"Find lines to match","type":"main","index":0}],[{"node":"Fetch official index","type":"main","index":0}],[{"node":"Build report","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Your receipts":{"main":[[{"node":"Settings","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Matches format":{"ai_outputParser":[[{"node":"Match new lines to products","type":"ai_outputParser","index":0}]]},"Receipt format":{"ai_outputParser":[[{"node":"Read receipt photo","type":"ai_outputParser","index":0}]]},"Speak the note":{"main":[[{"node":"Build report","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Gather receipts":{"main":[[{"node":"What came in?","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Gemini (writes)":{"ai_languageModel":[[{"node":"Write the economist's note","type":"ai_languageModel","index":0},{"node":"Note format","type":"ai_languageModel","index":0}]]},"Load saved lines":{"main":[[{"node":"Gather receipts","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Telegram receipts":{"main":[[{"node":"Settings","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Read receipt photo":{"main":[[{"node":"Find lines to match","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Save receipt lines":{"main":[[{"node":"Fetch official index","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Voice note wanted?":{"main":[[{"node":"Speak the note","type":"main","index":0}],[{"node":"Build report","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Find lines to match":{"main":[[{"node":"Anything new to match?","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Price matched lines":{"main":[[{"node":"Save receipt lines","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Fetch official index":{"main":[[{"node":"Calculate personal inflation","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Search saved products":{"ai_tool":[[{"node":"Match new lines to products","type":"ai_tool","index":0}]]},"Anything new to match?":{"main":[[{"node":"Match new lines to products","type":"main","index":0}],[{"node":"Price matched lines","type":"main","index":0}],[{"node":"Build report","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Reply where they asked":{"main":[[{"node":"Show the report","type":"main","index":0}],[{"node":"Telegram: send voice note","type":"main","index":0}],[{"node":"Telegram: send report","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Gemini (reads & matches)":{"ai_languageModel":[[{"node":"Read receipt photo","type":"ai_languageModel","index":0},{"node":"Receipt format","type":"ai_languageModel","index":0},{"node":"Match new lines to products","type":"ai_languageModel","index":0},{"node":"Matches format","type":"ai_languageModel","index":0}]]},"Telegram: send voice note":{"main":[[{"node":"Telegram: send report","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Create receipt lines table":{"main":[[{"node":"Load saved lines","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Write the economist's note":{"main":[[{"node":"Voice note wanted?","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Match new lines to products":{"main":[[{"node":"Price matched lines","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Calculate personal inflation":{"main":[[{"node":"Write the economist's note","type":"main","index":0}]]}}}